- !<Text/20392ef4-4ee3-48c5-9c5d-9778c4c77af7>
  PrefabRemaps:
    []
  Name: Text
  Enabled: true
  RenderOrder: 999
  StretchMode: Stretch
  VerticalAlignment: Top
  HorizontalAlignment: Left
  MeshShadowMode: None
  ShadowColor: {x: 1.000000, y: 1.000000, z: 1.000000, w: 1.000000}
  ShadowDensity: 1.000000
  Text: |-
    Agent Manager
    
    Manage AI coding agents in AR on Specs. Chat via
    text or voice, attach images with hand gestures, and
    see live agent status as 3D robot avatars pinned in
    your world.
    
    Before you start
    Complete the red setup warnings shown to the LEFT:
    - Assign your SupabaseProject asset on the
      SnapCloudRequirements object (Window > Supabase >
      Import Credentials, then drag the asset in)
    - Set your API token on RemoteServiceGatewayCredentials
    
    Requirements
    - Node.js 18+
    - Git with LFS
    - Claude CLI, Codex CLI, or OpenClaw
    
    Setup
    
    1. Supabase backend
       brew install supabase/tap/supabase
       supabase login --profile snap
       cd supabase && ./setup.sh
    
    2. Start the Bridge (.env is written by setup.sh)
       cd ../Bridge && npm install
       node sync.js
    
    3. Open in Lens Studio
       Open AgentManager.esproj. To test without a backend,
       set useMockData = true on AgentManagerController.
    
    4. Deploy & Pair
       Push the Lens to your Specs, then enter the 6-digit
       pairing code from the Bridge terminal (no API key
       needed for local agents).
